{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795248667,"nonce":"e+a+jDce793TEf+VkqZmjH5t/B0=","title":"Inset box shadows reach only stylesheet rules, not the builder or Div::set_style","message":"Only a parsed `box-shadow` fills `ElementStyle::inner_shadow`; no `ElementStyle` builder method sets it. `Div` has no inset field, so `Div::set_style` and `Div::merge` drop an inset from an `ElementStyle` (for example one made by `css!`), and the node renders without it. Stylesheet rules apply it to `RenderProps` directly, which is the path 773d78c fixed.\n\nNeeds an inset field on `Div` carried into `RenderProps`, `set_style`/`merge` treating the two lists as one value as `RenderProps::merge_from` does, and a builder entry point.","files":null}]}